<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Sun Notch Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:311-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="42.896827" lon="-122.133714"><ele>1973.4</ele><name>Park Headquarters parking</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:crater-lake-park-headquarters (OSM way 208653507); confidence: high; pdf_page: 313; book_elev_ft: 6475; quote: From the parking area at Park Headquarters (6,475 feet) ski east 1.7 miles to the trail's high point</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.880130" lon="-122.116930"><ele>2069.4</ele><name>Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive)</name><desc>source: as in 312-3: OSM East Rim Drive node 40187236, start of the DEM high stretch; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 313; book_elev_ft: 6806; quote: ski east 1.7 miles to the trail's high point after an initial descent then the long climb of over 400 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.884203" lon="-122.099242"><ele>2009.2</ele><name>Vidae Falls (Grayback / Motor Nature Road junction)</name><desc>source: OSM node where East Rim Drive way 222609400 meets Grayback Road way 222609394; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 314; quote: Continue on the Rim Road 0.7 mile to Crater Peak Trail ... and in 0.6 mile reach Vidae Falls and Motor Nature Road to the right</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.899707" lon="-122.095212"><ele>2143.8</ele><name>Sun Notch (Rim Drive at the trailhead)</name><desc>source: OSM node 10784949154, East Rim Drive at the Sun Notch trailhead service road; confidence: high; pdf_page: 314; book_elev_ft: 7115; quote: the Rim Road to Sun Notch, now only 1.3 miles from Vidae Falls and a 600-foot climb away ... Sun Notch at 7,115 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.902933" lon="-122.095960"><ele>2185.0</ele><name>Sun Notch viewpoint</name><desc>source: OSM Sun Notch Trail way 444357134, its northernmost node at the rim; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 313; quote: From the Rim Road you climb 400 yards up through old-growth forest to the Crater Lake viewpoint below the impressive Applegate cliffs</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Sun Notch Trail</name><desc>1. Park Headquarters parking -&gt; Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive): osm (high), 1.81 mi | 2. Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive) -&gt; Vidae Falls (Grayback / Motor Nature Road junction): osm (high), 1.32 mi | 3. Vidae Falls (Grayback / Motor Nature Road junction) -&gt; Sun Notch (Rim Drive at the trailhead): osm (high), 1.37 mi | 4. Sun Notch (Rim Drive at the trailhead) -&gt; Sun Notch viewpoint: osm (medium), 0.41 mi</desc>
